-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Dizzy - The Ultimate Cartoon Adventure
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1987
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy - The Ultimate Cartoon Adventure (1987)(Code Masters).z80
  MD5         0659328fd54fd446e39d1740bafd02e7

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Jao Paulo's colours: a yellow Dizzy, olive and yellow tree tops
              over brown trunks, timber huts and fences, dark grass on brown
              earth, a pale green castle and blazing orange dead trees; the
              panel and score unchanged. Source: Enhanced colours: Jao Paulo
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original (+0.86% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; three
              rooms, three seeds, at the player's own update, all 251 states
              matched per trial; positive is slower than the original)

  Changes     1.1: works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11); the hooks hand
              back the CPU speed the game was running at, at the original's
              pace. 1.2: Enhanced colours from Jao Paulo's Spec256 conversion,
              off by default; Sinclair's whole 48K ROM as the alt ROM, so the
              game's ROM reads get the right bytes; R kept as the original's
              at every hook; faster particle and scenery drawing. The default
              look is unchanged.

  Note        Keys: Z and X walk, Space jumps and starts the game, P pauses.
              The default keeps the published look: the game's own colours
              with the clash removed. Enhanced repaints Dizzy, the scenery,
              creatures and items in Jao Paulo's Spec256 colours; off by
              default. The patch carries Sinclair's whole 48K ROM, so it runs
              on NextZXOS 26.11. The original 48K game with its beeper sound;
              fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: the game's own screen-copy and
              rotate effects stay in Spectrum colours; a room redraw can show
              a brief attribute change, slightly more than the original does
              (18 cells against 12 in testing); in JNext quiet play runs from
              1.8 percent faster to 0.9 percent slower than the original, busy
              scenes from 2.8 percent faster to 1.3 percent slower. Missing:
              natural play to the end was not reached in testing; the
              archive's cheats that ask for a value (Lives, Walk Speed);
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity
   3  Walk through walls
   4  Forest floor holds

  The archive's Dizzy.pok. Its Infinite Lives address (62745) is wrong for
  this release; the patch uses the DEC A at 62746. Left out: Lives and Walk
  Speed, which ask for a value.

